# DEBT-0015 — Control Plane Duplication Between In-Memory CLI and Self-Host Drivers

**Status**: OPEN  
**Filed**: 2026-07-30  
**Priority**: Low  
**Category**: Duplicated Mechanisms / Hidden Coupling  

---

## 1. Compromise
In [cli/paeos.py](file:///Users/bob/GitHub/paeos/cli/paeos.py), `ControlPlane` manages in-memory ledger and CAS instances for `paeos demo`, while `_self_host` in `cli/paeos.py` and `run_backlog` in [runtime/selfhost.py](file:///Users/bob/GitHub/paeos/runtime/selfhost.py) independently instantiate `SqliteLedgerStore` and `FilesystemCasStore`, duplicating store initialization, key loading, and evidence handling logic.

## 2. Reason
`ControlPlane` was implemented in B0.12 for in-memory single-process goal driving. When self-hosting backlog runs were introduced in B2.B/C, `runtime/selfhost.py` and `_self_host` constructed persistent SQLite and filesystem backends directly.

## 3. Ideal Solution
Refactor `ControlPlane` in `cli/paeos.py` to accept pluggable persistence backends (SQLite/Filesystem CAS) and unify all CLI execution commands (`demo`, `self-host`, `calibrate`, `amend`) through `ControlPlane`.

## 4. Repayment Conditions
Repay during Phase 3 CLI control plane consolidation.

## 5. Estimated Impact
Low. Multiple entry points for setting up CAS, Ledger, and signing keys increases maintenance overhead and creates minor coupling between CLI wrappers and storage implementations.
